# BFF — Public price list (no JWT)
# UC-128: GET /v1/public/billing/prices?country=, the price table of /ikaro-trial.
# Cacheable for five minutes (Cache-Control: public, max-age=300) on a 200 only: a 400 or 503 never
# carries it. Enums and amounts in minor units, no display string and no tenant field. A country a
# visitor cannot sign up from (the US until M28, or an unknown one) is 200 { "items": [] }.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. pnpm infra:up
#   2. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run migration:run
#   3. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run dev  (port 3001)
#   4. pnpm --filter @ikaro/bff run dev      (port 3002)
#
# REST Client environment: select "local" in the VS Code status bar.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HAPPY PATH
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Brazil → 200 { countryCode, currency, taxBehavior: "INCLUSIVE", items: [{ featureKey, tier, amountMinor, upcoming? }] }
GET {{bffUrl}}/v1/public/billing/prices?country=BR

### The query string is part of the cache key: a lowercase code is a separate cache entry, same answer
GET {{bffUrl}}/v1/public/billing/prices?country=br

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT OFFERED (200, never an error)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### The US → 200 { "items": [] }
GET {{bffUrl}}/v1/public/billing/prices?country=US

### An unknown country → 200 { "items": [] }
GET {{bffUrl}}/v1/public/billing/prices?country=ZZ

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ERRORS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Malformed country → 400 COUNTRY_CODE_FORMAT_INVALID (passed through from the backend)
GET {{bffUrl}}/v1/public/billing/prices?country=B1

### Missing country → 400 (the BFF checks only that it is present)
GET {{bffUrl}}/v1/public/billing/prices
